// What did remote write actually create?
//
// Run this before writing any other query. Note what it says about
// transactions and shares_traded: Elasticsearch infers metric type from the
// NAME SUFFIX, and neither carries _total, so both arrive as GAUGES. RATE()
// does not apply to them. When you need a rate, use a counter such as
// http_requests_total.
TS ${DATA_STREAM}
| WHERE TRANGE(30 minutes)
| METRICS_INFO
| WHERE metric_name LIKE "*transactions*" OR metric_name LIKE "*shares*"
     OR metric_name LIKE "*http_request*" OR metric_name LIKE "*redis_up*"
| KEEP metric_name, metric_type, field_type
| SORT metric_name
| LIMIT 20
